terraform force-unlock LOCK_ID               This removes the lock.    ⚠️ Don't use it blindly because another Terraform process may actually be running.
Terraform can use state locking to prevent two people/processes from modifying the same state at the same time.
For example:
Developer A
    ↓
terraform apply
    ↓
State LOCKED

If Developer B tries:  terraform apply
Terraform may say: Error: state is locked
Normally, when Developer A's operation finishes, the lock is automatically released.
But sometimes a failed/crashed process can leave a stale lock.
Then an administrator can use:  terraform force-unlock LOCK_ID
This manually removes the lock.
⚠️ Very dangerous if used incorrectly.
You should only force-unlock when you're certain that no other Terraform operation is currently running.



